srow(306, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND LET THE EARTH HEAR THE WORDS OF MY MOUTH" — LOOK AT THE EARTH I CREATED TO SERVE YOU: HAS IT CHANGED ITS MEASURE? DID YOU SOW AND IT DID NOT SPROUT, SOW WHEAT AND IT RAISED BARLEY? HAS THIS COW SAID: I WILL NOT THRESH NOR PLOW TODAY, OR THIS ASS: I WILL NOT CARRY NOR GO? SO OF THE SEA — "WILL YOU NOT FEAR ME … WHO SET THE SAND A BOUND FOR THE SEA" (Jeremiah 5:22): SINCE I DECREED IT HAS IT CHANGED ITS MEASURE AND SAID I WILL RISE AND FLOOD THE WORLD? RATHER "I BROKE MY DECREE UPON IT, SET BAR AND DOORS, AND SAID: THUS FAR YOU SHALL COME AND NO FURTHER" (Job 38:10-11), AND MORE — IT GRIEVES AND KNOWS NOT WHAT TO DO ("THEY TOSS AND CANNOT"). AND IS IT NOT AN A-FORTIORI: THESE, MADE NEITHER FOR REWARD NOR FOR LOSS — WORTHY THEY GET NO REWARD, SINNING THEY GET NO PUNISHMENT, THEY PITY NOT THEIR SONS AND DAUGHTERS — HAVE NOT CHANGED THEIR MEASURE; YOU, WHO ARE REWARDED WHEN WORTHY AND PUNISHED WHEN YOU SIN AND PITY YOUR SONS AND DAUGHTERS — HOW MUCH MORE MUST YOU NOT CHANGE YOUR MEASURES. ({SP_(306, 8, "הסתכלו", "בארץ", "שבראתי", "לשמשכם")} "look at the earth I created to serve you"; {SP_(306, 8, "שמא", "זרעתם", "חטים", "והעלת", "שעורים")} "did you sow wheat and it raised barley"; {SP_(306, 8, "ומה", "אלו", "שנעשו", "לא", "לשכר", "ולא", "להפסד")} "if these, made neither for reward nor for loss"): THE EARTH\'S AND THE SEA\'S UNCHANGED MEASURE and the a-fortiori (I1) to Israel — the unrewarded creation keeps its law, the rewarded people should the more; the compile: the natural order\'s constancy the frame of every law with reward attached (the blessing and the curse on the tape). The Prophets\' and the Writings\' seats cited, never read. DV32-01. Fresh.')
