srow(306, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'"MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP AS THE RAIN" (32:2) — MY DOCTRINE (likchi) IS ONLY WORDS OF TORAH: "FOR I GIVE YOU GOOD DOCTRINE, FORSAKE NOT MY TORAH" (Proverbs 4:2); "TAKE MY INSTRUCTION AND NOT SILVER" (Proverbs 8:10) — AND INSTRUCTION IS ONLY WORDS OF TORAH: "HEAR, MY SON, YOUR FATHER\'S INSTRUCTION AND FORSAKE NOT YOUR MOTHER\'S TORAH" (Proverbs 1:8), "HEAR INSTRUCTION AND BE WISE" (Proverbs 8:33), "HOLD FAST TO INSTRUCTION, LET IT NOT GO" (Proverbs 4:13); "TAKE WITH YOU WORDS AND RETURN" (Hosea 14:3) — AND WORDS ARE ONLY WORDS OF TORAH: "THESE WORDS THE LORD SPOKE TO ALL YOUR ASSEMBLY" (5:19). ({SP_(306, 16, "אין", "לקחי", "אלא", "דברי", "תורה")} "my doctrine is only words of Torah"; {SP_(306, 16, "ואין", "דברים", "אלא", "דברי", "תורה")} "and words are only words of Torah"): THE RAIN VERSE OPENED — its first noun fixed as Torah by a chain of Proverbs (the Writings\' seats cited, never read) closing on 5:19\'s "these words" — the Decalogue\'s words on the tape (the seat that read this row at chapter 5). The compile: the doctrine = the Torah, a definition the song\'s own word carries; no law (DV32-01). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 5\'s reading — 5:19).')
srow(306, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS THE RAIN" — AS THE RAIN IS LIFE TO THE WORLD SO WORDS OF TORAH ARE LIFE TO THE WORLD; OR AS THE RAIN — PART OF THE WORLD REJOICES IN IT AND PART GRIEVES (HE WHOSE CISTERN IS FULL OF WINE, WHOSE THRESHING FLOOR IS BEFORE HIM) — COULD WORDS OF TORAH BE SO? IT SAYS "MY SPEECH SHALL DISTIL AS THE DEW": AS ALL THE WORLD REJOICES IN THE DEW SO ALL THE WORLD REJOICES IN WORDS OF TORAH. ({SP_(306, 17, "מה", "מטר", "חיים", "לעולם", "אף", "דברי", "תורה")} "as the rain is life to the world so words of Torah"; {SP_(306, 17, "מה", "טל", "כל", "העולם", "שמחים", "בו")} "as all the world rejoices in the dew"): RAIN AND DEW — the second clause limits the first (the dew\'s universal welcome corrects the rain\'s mixed one): the verse read as a pair whose second member restricts the first (the compile\'s form: an inclusion then its guard; no law here). DV32-01. Fresh.')
srow(306, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS THE SMALL RAIN ON THE TENDER GRASS" — AS THESE SHOWERS COME DOWN ON THE HERBS AND RAISE THEM AND MAKE THEM GROW, SO WORDS OF TORAH RAISE YOU AND MAKE YOU GROW — "EXALT HER AND SHE WILL LIFT YOU UP" (Proverbs 4:8). ({SP_(306, 18, "כך", "דברי", "תורה", "מעלים", "אותך", "ומגדלים", "אותך")} "so words of Torah raise you and make you grow"): the third rain (se\'irim) read as growth; the Writings\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-01). Fresh.')
srow(306, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND AS THE SHOWERS ON THE HERB" — AS THESE SHOWERS COME DOWN ON THE HERBS AND DELIGHT THEM AND PAMPER THEM, SO WORDS OF TORAH DELIGHT YOU AND PAMPER YOU — "FOR THEY ARE A GARLAND OF GRACE TO YOUR HEAD" (Proverbs 1:9), "SHE WILL GIVE TO YOUR HEAD A GARLAND OF GRACE" (Proverbs 4:9). ({SP_(306, 19, "כך", "דברי", "תורה", "מעדנים", "אותך", "ומפנקים", "אותך")} "so words of Torah delight you and pamper you"): the fourth rain (revivim) read as delight — the four rains of 32:2 each a work of Torah on the student (306:16-19 the first cycle); the Writings\' seats cited, never read; no law (DV32-01). Fresh.')
srow(306, 20, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP AS THE RAIN" — R. NEHEMIAH USED TO SAY: ALWAYS GATHER WORDS OF TORAH AS GENERAL RULES; COULD YOU BRING THEM OUT AS GENERAL RULES AS YOU GATHERED THEM? IT SAYS "YA\'AROF AS THE RAIN" — AND YA\'AROF IS ONLY THE MERCHANT\'S TONGUE (leshon kena\'ani): A MAN DOES NOT SAY TO HIS FELLOW "CHANGE ME THIS SELA" BUT "AROF (BREAK) ME THIS SELA" — SO GATHER WORDS OF TORAH AS GENERAL RULES AND BREAK THEM OUT AS THESE DROPS OF DEW, NOT AS THESE DROPS OF RAIN WHICH ARE LARGE, BUT AS THE DROPS OF DEW WHICH ARE SMALL. ({SP_(306, 20, "לעולם", "הוי", "כונס", "דברי", "תורה", "כללים")} "always gather words of Torah as general rules"; {SP_(306, 20, "ואין", "יערף", "אלא", "לשון", "כנעני")} "and ya\'arof is only the merchant\'s tongue"; {SP_(306, 20, "ערוף", "לי", "סלע", "זה")} "break me this sela"): THE RARE VERB READ BY THE MARKETPLACE — ya\'arof (drop) as \'break into small change\': learn in generals, teach in particulars, small as dew (the compile\'s own method named by the spine: the general rule compiled, the cases printed one by one). The translator\'s note on the merchant sense of kena\'ani (Zechariah 14:21, Proverbs 31:24 cited). DV32-01. Fresh.')
srow(306, 21, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS THE SMALL RAIN ON THE TENDER GRASS" — AS THESE SHOWERS COME DOWN ON THE HERBS AND SEARCH THROUGH THEM SO THEY DO NOT GET WORMY, SO SEARCH THROUGH WORDS OF TORAH SO YOU DO NOT FORGET THEM; SO R. YAAKOV SON OF R. CHANILAI SAID TO RABBI: COME, LET US SEARCH THROUGH THE LAWS SO THEY DO NOT RUST. ({SP_(306, 21, "כך", "הוי", "מפשפש", "בדברי", "תורה", "כדי", "שלא")} "so search through words of Torah so that you do not"; {SP_(306, 21, "בוא", "ונפשפש", "בהלכות", "כדי", "שלא", "יעלו", "חלודה")} "come, let us search the laws so they do not rust"): review against forgetting — the second cycle (306:20-22) on the four rains as the method of study; the compile: the sweep\'s own duty in the tradition\'s words (the gates rerun so the laws do not rust). DV32-01. Fresh.')
srow(306, 22, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND AS THE SHOWERS ON THE HERB" — AS THESE SHOWERS COME DOWN ON THE HERBS AND CLEANSE THEM AND FATTEN THEM, SO FATTEN WORDS OF TORAH — REPEAT, AND A THIRD TIME, AND A FOURTH. ({SP_(306, 22, "כך", "הוי", "מפטם", "דברי", "תורה", "ושונה", "ומשלש")} "so fatten words of Torah — repeat, a third time"): repetition to the fourth — the count of reviews a parameter the tradition sets (the Babylonian Talmud Eruvin 54b\'s four the testing shelf, cited); no law (DV32-01). Fresh.')
