srow(306, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS THE SMALL RAIN (se\'irim) ON THE TENDER GRASS" — FOR WHAT DO THE GOATS (se\'irim) ATONE? FOR SINS (chataot); SO WORDS OF TORAH ATONE FOR SINS; "AND AS THE SHOWERS ON THE HERB" — AS THE SHOWERS COME WHOLE (temimim) AND ATONE, SO WORDS OF TORAH ATONE FOR ALL INIQUITIES AND TRANSGRESSIONS. ({SP_(306, 24, "ועל", "מה", "שעירים", "מכפרים", "על", "חטאות")} "and for what do goats atone — for sins"; {SP_(306, 24, "מה", "רביבים", "באים", "תמימים", "ומכפרים")} "as the showers come whole and atone"): THE HOMOGRAPH READ — se\'irim the small rains and se\'irim the goats (the sin-offering goats of Numbers 28:15 — the translator\'s seat; the compile: the goat\'s atonement on the tape at the festivals\' offerings, a homograph the parser must not follow: the rain is not the goat); the pun carried, the law not moved. DV32-01. Fresh.')
srow(306, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP AS THE RAIN" — THE SAGES SAY: MOSES SAID TO ISRAEL, DO YOU NOT KNOW HOW MUCH I SUFFERED FOR THE TORAH, HOW MUCH I LABORED AND WEARIED IN IT — "AND HE WAS THERE WITH THE LORD FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS" (Exodus 34:28), "AND I SAT ON THE MOUNTAIN FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS" (9:9); I WENT IN AMONG THE ANGELS, AMONG THE LIVING CREATURES, AMONG THE SERAPHIM ONE OF WHOM COULD BURN THE WHOLE WORLD (Isaiah 6:2); MY SOUL I GAVE FOR IT, MY BLOOD I GAVE FOR IT — AS I LEARNED IT IN PAIN SHALL YOU LEARN IT IN PAIN? OR AS YOU LEARN IT IN PAIN SHALL YOU TEACH IT IN PAIN? IT SAYS "MY SPEECH SHALL DISTIL (tizal) AS THE DEW" — SEE IT AS THOUGH IT WERE CHEAP (bezol): ONE OF THREE OR FOUR SEAHS FOR A SELA. ({SP_(306, 25, "כמה", "צער", "נצטערתי", "על", "התורה")} "how much I suffered for the Torah"; {SP_(306, 25, "נפשי", "נתתי", "עליה", "דמי", "נתתי", "עליה")} "my soul I gave for it, my blood I gave for it"; {SP_(306, 25, "תהו", "רואים", "אותה", "כאלו", "היא", "בזול")} "see it as though it were cheap"): MOSES\' FORTY DAYS as the price and the dew as the cheapness — 9:9\'s forty days the seat that read this row at chapter 9 (the tape\'s own count, a RUN CITATION with Exodus 34:28); the pun tizal / bezol (distil / cheap) the translator\'s note; the compile: no law (DV32-01). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 9\'s reading — 9:9).')
