srow(306, 33, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: AS THIS RAIN YOU DO NOT SEE UNTIL IT COMES — "AND IT CAME TO PASS IN A LITTLE WHILE THAT THE HEAVENS GREW BLACK WITH CLOUDS" (1 Kings 18:45) — SO A DISCIPLE OF THE SAGES YOU KNOW NOT WHAT HE IS UNTIL HE REPEATS MIDRASH (SCRIPTURAL EXPOSITION), LAWS AND LORE, OR UNTIL HE IS APPOINTED ADMINISTRATOR OVER THE COMMUNITY. ({SP_(306, 33, "כך", "תלמיד", "חכמים", "אין", "אתה", "יודע", "מה")} "so a disciple of the sages — you know not what"; {SP_(306, 33, "עד", "שיתמנה", "פרנס", "על", "הצבור")} "until he is appointed administrator over the community"): the scholar known by his output or his office; the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; no law (DV32-01). Fresh.')
srow(306, 34, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP AS THE RAIN" — NOT AS THE RAIN THAT COMES FROM THE SOUTH, ALL BLIGHT AND MILDEW AND CURSE, BUT AS THE RAIN THAT COMES FROM THE WEST, ALL BLESSING. R. SIMAI USED TO SAY: WHENCE THAT AS MOSES CALLED HEAVEN AND EARTH TO WITNESS AGAINST ISRAEL SO HE CALLED THE FOUR WINDS OF HEAVEN? "YA\'AROF AS THE RAIN MY DOCTRINE" — THE WEST WIND, THE BACK (oref) OF THE WORLD, ALL BLESSING; "MY SPEECH SHALL DISTIL AS THE DEW" — THE NORTH WIND THAT MAKES THE SKY CLEAN AS GOLD; "AS THE SMALL RAIN (se\'irim) ON THE TENDER GRASS" — THE EAST WIND THAT BLACKENS THE SKY LIKE GOATS; "AND AS THE SHOWERS (revivim) ON THE HERB" — THE SOUTH WIND THAT WEAVES THE SKY LIKE A CLOUD. ({SP_(306, 34, "לא", "כמטר", "זה", "שבא", "מן", "הדרום")} "not as the rain that comes from the south"; {SP_(306, 34, "כך", "העיד", "בהם", "ארבע", "רוחות", "השמים")} "so he called the four winds of heaven to witness against them"; {SP_(306, 34, "זו", "רוח", "מערבית", "שהיא", "ערפו", "של", "עולם")} "this is the west wind, the back of the world"): THE FOUR RAINS AS THE FOUR WINDS — a third reading of ya\'arof (the west is the world\'s nape); the four winds joined to heaven and earth as witnesses (six witnesses in R. Simai\'s count); the compile: the winds\' seasons the land\'s clock (the calendar\'s parameters), no law (DV32-01). Fresh.')
srow(306, 35, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP AS THE RAIN" — AND SO R. SIMAI USED TO SAY: THESE FOUR WINDS WERE SAID ONLY AGAINST THE FOUR WINDS OF HEAVEN — THE NORTH FAIR IN THE SUNNY DAYS AND HARSH IN THE RAINY, THE SOUTH HARSH IN THE SUNNY AND FAIR IN THE RAINY, THE EAST ALWAYS HARSH, THE WEST ALWAYS FAIR; THE NORTH FAIR FOR THE WHEAT AT A THIRD AND HARSH FOR THE OLIVES AT BUDDING, THE SOUTH THE REVERSE. AND SO R. SIMAI USED TO SAY: ALL CREATURES CREATED FROM THE HEAVENS — THEIR SOUL AND BODY ARE FROM THE HEAVENS; ALL CREATED FROM THE EARTH — FROM THE EARTH; EXCEPT MAN, WHOSE SOUL IS FROM THE HEAVENS AND BODY FROM THE EARTH: IF HE DOES TORAH AND HIS FATHER\'S WILL IN HEAVEN HE IS AS THE CREATURES ABOVE — "I SAID: YOU ARE GODS, SONS OF THE MOST HIGH ALL OF YOU" (Psalm 82:6); IF NOT, AS THE CREATURES BELOW — "SURELY AS ADAM YOU SHALL DIE" (Psalm 82:7). AND SO R. SIMAI USED TO SAY: THERE IS NO SECTION WITHOUT THE RESURRECTION OF THE DEAD, ONLY WE LACK THE STRENGTH TO EXPOUND — "HE CALLS TO THE HEAVENS ABOVE AND TO THE EARTH TO JUDGE HIS PEOPLE" (Psalm 50:4): TO THE HEAVENS ABOVE — THE SOUL; TO THE EARTH — THE BODY, TO BE JUDGED WITH IT; AND WHENCE THAT IT SPEAKS OF THE RESURRECTION — "COME FROM THE FOUR WINDS, O BREATH, AND BREATHE ON THESE SLAIN" (Ezekiel 37:9). ({SP_(306, 35, "מזרחית", "לעולם", "קשה", "מערבית", "לעולם", "יפה")} "the east always harsh, the west always fair"; {SP_(306, 35, "חוץ", "מאדם", "זה", "שנפשו", "מן", "השמים")} "except man, whose soul is from the heavens"; {SP_(306, 35, "אין", "לך", "פרשה", "שאין", "בה", "תחית", "מתים")} "there is no section without the resurrection of the dead"): THE WINDS\' AGRONOMY (the Mekhilta on Exodus 14 the parallel, cited), MAN OF HEAVEN AND EARTH (the two witnesses his two parts — the song\'s summons a summons of the hearer\'s own soul and body), and THE RESURRECTION IN EVERY SECTION (Psalm 50:4 revoweled to \'to be judged with it\' — the translator\'s note): the compile: no law — the resurrection a declared future outside the tape\'s clock (the Writings\' and the Prophets\' seats cited, never read). DV32-01. Fresh.')
srow(306, 36, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR I WILL PROCLAIM THE NAME OF THE LORD" (32:3) — WE FIND THAT MOSES DID NOT MENTION THE NAME OF THE HOLY ONE UNTIL AFTER TWENTY-ONE WORDS; FROM WHOM DID HE LEARN? FROM THE MINISTERING ANGELS, WHO MENTION THE NAME ONLY AFTER THREE SANCTIFICATIONS — "AND ONE CALLED TO ANOTHER AND SAID: HOLY, HOLY, HOLY IS THE LORD OF HOSTS" (Isaiah 6:3); MOSES SAID: IT IS ENOUGH THAT I BE AT SEVEN TIMES THE MINISTERING ANGELS. AND IS IT NOT AN A-FORTIORI: IF MOSES, THE WISEST OF THE WISE, THE GREATEST OF THE GREAT, THE FATHER OF THE PROPHETS, DID NOT MENTION THE NAME OF THE PLACE UNTIL AFTER TWENTY-ONE WORDS, HE WHO MENTIONS THE NAME OF THE PLACE IN VAIN, HOW MUCH MORE. R. SHIMON BEN YOCHAI SAYS: WHENCE THAT A MAN SHALL NOT SAY "TO THE LORD A BURNT OFFERING", "TO THE LORD A MEAL OFFERING", "TO THE LORD PEACE OFFERINGS", BUT "A BURNT OFFERING TO THE LORD", "A MEAL OFFERING TO THE LORD", "PEACE OFFERINGS TO THE LORD"? IT SAYS "AN OFFERING TO THE LORD" (Leviticus 1:2); AND IS IT NOT AN A-FORTIORI: IF OF THESE, CONSECRATED TO HEAVEN, THE HOLY ONE SAID MY NAME SHALL NOT REST ON THEM UNTIL THEY ARE CONSECRATED, HE WHO MENTIONS THE NAME OF THE HOLY ONE IN VAIN AND IN A PLACE OF CONTEMPT, HOW MUCH MORE. ({SP_(306, 36, "שלא", "הזכיר", "משה", "שמו", "של", "הקדוש", "ברוך")} "that Moses did not mention the name of the Holy One, blessed"; {SP_(306, 36, "אלא", "לאחר", "עשרים", "ואחד", "דבר")} "until after twenty-one words"; {SP_(306, 36, "המזכיר", "שמו", "של", "מקום", "בחנם")} "he who mentions the name of the Place in vain"): THE NAME VERSE OPENED — TWENTY-ONE WORDS before the Name in 32:1-3 (the count the ink can compute at the compile: the Name\'s first seat at 32:3\'s third token; the measure counts the Name seven times bare in the chapter), seven times the angels\' three (Isaiah 6:3); and THE OFFERING FORMULA\'S WORD ORDER from Leviticus 1:2 (the Sifra on Leviticus 1:2 the parallel, cited — the Sifra\'s rule compiled at the offerings\' span on the tape; the Mishnah Nedarim 1:2\'s vow formulas the testing shelf, cited): the compile: the Name uttered after praise a rule of speech, no verdict; the formula\'s order a parameter of the offering\'s declaration (DV32-01). Fresh.')
srow(306, 37, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR I WILL PROCLAIM THE NAME OF THE LORD" (32:3) — R. YOSE SAYS: WHENCE THAT WHEN THOSE STANDING IN THE SYNAGOGUE SAY "BLESS THE LORD WHO IS BLESSED" THE OTHERS ANSWER "BLESSED IS THE LORD WHO IS BLESSED FOR EVER AND EVER"? "FOR I WILL PROCLAIM THE NAME OF THE LORD — ASCRIBE GREATNESS TO OUR GOD". R. NEHORAI SAID TO HIM: BY HEAVEN! IT IS THE WAY OF THE WORLD — THE FOOT SOLDIERS PROVOKE THE BATTLE AND THE MIGHTY WIN. AND WHENCE THAT THE BLESSING AFTER THE MEAL IS CONVENED ONLY WITH THREE? "FOR I WILL PROCLAIM … ASCRIBE (plural) GREATNESS TO OUR GOD"; AND WHENCE THAT ONE ANSWERS AMEN AFTER THE ONE WHO BLESSES? "ASCRIBE GREATNESS TO OUR GOD"; AND WHENCE THAT ONE SAYS "BLESSED BE THE NAME OF HIS GLORIOUS KINGDOM FOR EVER AND EVER"? "FOR I WILL PROCLAIM THE NAME OF THE LORD"; AND WHENCE THAT TO THOSE WHO SAY "MAY HIS GREAT NAME BE BLESSED" ONE ANSWERS "FOR EVER AND TO ALL ETERNITY"? "ASCRIBE GREATNESS TO OUR GOD". AND WHENCE THAT OUR FATHERS WENT DOWN TO EGYPT ONLY THAT THE HOLY ONE MIGHT DO THEM MIRACLES AND MIGHTY DEEDS TO SANCTIFY HIS GREAT NAME IN THE WORLD (Exodus 2:23-24)? AND THE TEN PLAGUES ON PHARAOH AND EGYPT ONLY TO SANCTIFY HIS NAME — "WHO IS THE LORD THAT I SHOULD HEED HIM" (Exodus 5:2) AT THE START, "THE LORD IS RIGHTEOUS AND I AND MY PEOPLE ARE WICKED" (Exodus 9:27) AT THE END; AND THE MIRACLES AT THE SEA, THE JORDAN AND THE VALLEYS OF ARNON (Joshua 5:1; Rahab, Joshua 2:10); AND DANIEL INTO THE LIONS\' DEN (Daniel 6:27) AND CHANANIAH, MISHAEL AND AZARIAH INTO THE FURNACE (Daniel 3:32-33) — ALL TO SANCTIFY HIS GREAT NAME; AND WHENCE THAT THE MINISTERING ANGELS DO NOT MENTION THE NAME ABOVE UNTIL ISRAEL MENTION IT BELOW? "HEAR, O ISRAEL, THE LORD OUR GOD, THE LORD IS ONE" (6:4), AND "WHEN THE MORNING STARS SANG TOGETHER" — ISRAEL, LIKENED TO THE STARS (Genesis 22:17) — AND THEN "ALL THE SONS OF GOD SHOUTED" (Job 38:7) — THE MINISTERING ANGELS (Job 1:6). ({SP_(306, 37, "ומנין", "שאין", "מזמנים", "אלא", "בשלשה")} "and whence that the meal blessing is convened only with three"; {SP_(306, 37, "ומנין", "שעונים", "אמן", "אחר", "המברך")} "and whence that one answers Amen after the one who blesses"; {SP_(306, 37, "שאין", "מלאכי", "השרת", "מזכירים", "שמו")} "that the ministering angels do not mention His name"): THE SYNAGOGUE\'S RESPONSES FROM ONE VERSE — Barekhu and its answer, THE ZIMMUN OF THREE (Mishnah Berakhot 7:1 — the translator\'s seat), Amen after a blessing (Berakhot 8:8), "Blessed be the name of His glorious kingdom" inside the Shema (Berakhot 2:2 — the Shema\'s paragraphs; 6:4 the seat that read this row at chapter 6), the Kaddish\'s answer — the answer sheet\'s rows the compile takes as cases (the testing shelf, cited); THE NAME SANCTIFIED BY HISTORY — Egypt, the plagues, the sea, the Jordan, the Arnon (the tape\'s own entries, RUN CITATIONS), Daniel and the three (the Writings\' seats cited, never read); THE ANGELS WAIT FOR ISRAEL (6:4 the trigger). The compile at 20b: the response formulas parameters of the liturgy\'s law (a status on the assembly of three), the Name\'s sanctification a status the tape\'s miracles write (DV32-01). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 6\'s reading — 6:4).')
